KG42.register("rules-b35aeb0065d7da5dd2165b93",{"id":"18-dlmp_analysis::v141-c-R002","paper":"18-dlmp_analysis","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R002","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local clearing price","process_stage":"pricing","market_meaning":"Clearing low-voltage local markets determines real-power DLMPs at individual distribution nodes. Scope: The common approach described for [4], [7], and [11]–[14]: real-power pricing at individual distribution nodes in low-voltage local markets. Condition: Given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function pricing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R002-E001","source":"clearing.local","target":"pricing.local","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"The common approach described for [4], [7], and [11]–[14]: real-power pricing at individual distribution nodes in low-voltage local markets.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Clearing low-voltage local markets determines real-power DLMPs at individual distribution nodes. Scope: The common approach described for [4], [7], and [11]–[14]: real-power pricing at individual distribution nodes in low-voltage local markets. Condition: Given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E003"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","location":{"location_id":"src-b1966ef5f7-p01-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":1,"printed_page":null,"section":"I. Introduction","anchor_text":"ure p , p , he such that the reserves can be delivered by distributed resources uf- while respecting","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-01.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A related question is how distribution locational marginal prices should be computed. In this respect, the common approach adopted in [4], [7], and [11]–[14] is the following: (i) locational marginal prices of high-voltage buses (TLMPs) are determined by clearing transmission markets, and (ii) DSOs clear local markets in the low-voltage grid in order to determine distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) for real power at the level of individual distribution nodes, given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"No rule-scoped algebraic decision variable is defined by the supplied evidence. The quotation names market operations (local market clearing and DLMP determination) and a TLMP condition, not an optimization variable; OPF decision variables elsewhere in the paper belong to other M03 rules and are not moved into this rule.","empty_theta_reason":"The supplied evidence defines no parameter, coefficient, constant, value, unit, or index set for this pricing step. Although the prose says local clearing is conditional on the corresponding TLMP, this rule's evidence provides no typed TLMP parameter object or notation to formalize without inventing a symbol definition."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E003","quote":"DSOs clear local markets in the low-voltage grid in order to determine distribution locational marginal prices (DLMPs) for real power at the level of individual distribution nodes, given the TLMP of the corresponding transmission buses."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2cb64bd4146fbdb12927576590d1c77425a122187fedb586f2188dc4666570ec","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The supplied, still-unreviewed evidence describes a procedural pricing step: TLMPs are set by transmission-market clearing, and DSOs clear low-voltage local markets to determine real-power DLMPs at individual distribution nodes given the corresponding TLMP. It gives no algebraic equation, decision variable, parameter definition, or constraint for this rule. The frozen graph exposes only clearing.local and pricing.local, so there are no rule-scoped x/theta objects. Mathematical DLMP expressions elsewhere in the paper belong to the separate M03 implicit-function/SOCP rules and are not transferred here.","bindings":[],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
